<figure id="S5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>MIAs against tokenizers with the min count defense. Here, <math id="S5.T6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes a threshold. If a token appears fewer than <math id="S5.T6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{\text{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{\text{min}}</annotation></semantics></math> times in training data, it is likely a distinctive token and will be excluded from the vocabulary <math id="S5.T6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="S5.T6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|\leq 80{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>80,000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|\leq 80{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> indicates the vocabulary size prior to applying defense is 80,000. BA denotes balanced accuracy. TPR refers to TPR @ 1.0% FPR.</figcaption>
