<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.12" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.742</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.13" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">35.00%</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.14" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.748</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.15" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.746</td>
<td id="A0.T11.2.1.8.16" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">38.75%</td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Theorem</h2>

<div id="Thmmanualtheoremx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_manualtheorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.2 (RTF-SI under the Power Law)</span></span><span id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the power-law distribution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">[</span><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a><span id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">]</span></cite>, the frequency <math id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})</annotation></semantics></math> of a token <math id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\in\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">target</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\in\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> is proportional to <math id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/i^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/i^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\propto\frac{1}{i^{\alpha}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\propto\frac{1}{i^{\alpha}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&gt;x_{\textup{min}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&gt;x_{\textup{min}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math> , <math id="Thmmanualtheoremx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\textup{min}}\in\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℤ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\textup{min}}\in\mathbb{Z}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math> are constants defined by the power law.
Then, RTF-SI can be approximated by its lower bound:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{RTF\text{-}SI}(D,t_{i},\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\geq\frac{n_{D}(t_{i})}{\sum_{D^{\prime}\in\mathbb{D}}n_{D^{\prime}}(t_{i})}\cdot\log(\hskip-8.99994pt\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\hskip-8.99994pt{i^{\alpha}}/{j^{\alpha}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>RTF</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>SI</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{RTF\text{-}SI}(D,t_{i},\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\geq\frac{n_{D}(t_{i})}{\sum_{D^{\prime}\in\mathbb{D}}n_{D^{\prime}}(t_{i})}\cdot\log(\hskip-8.99994pt\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\hskip-8.99994pt{i^{\alpha}}/{j^{\alpha}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Given that <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\propto\frac{1}{i^{\alpha}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\propto\frac{1}{i^{\alpha}}</annotation></semantics></math>, let us assume</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})=C/i^{\alpha}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})=C/i^{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\in\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\in\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant. Since the sum of the frequencies <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}\in\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}\in\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> is at most 1, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\geq\hskip-3.00003pt\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\Pr(t_{j}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})=\hskip-3.00003pt\sum_{j=1+x_{\textup{min}}}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\hskip-6.99997pt{C}/{j^{\alpha}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\geq\hskip-3.00003pt\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\Pr(t_{j}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})=\hskip-3.00003pt\sum_{j=1+x_{\textup{min}}}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\hskip-6.99997pt{C}/{j^{\alpha}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the upper bound for the constant <math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\leq\frac{1}{\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\frac{1}{j^{\alpha}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>j</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\leq\frac{1}{\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\frac{1}{j^{\alpha}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Using Equations <a href="#A1.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Membership Inference Attacks on Tokenizers of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> and <a href="#A1.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix A Proof of Theorem ‣ Membership Inference Attacks on Tokenizers of Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>, we derive the upper bound for the frequency <math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\leq\frac{1}{\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\frac{1}{j^{\alpha}}}\cdot\frac{1}{i^{\alpha}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>j</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\leq\frac{1}{\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\frac{1}{j^{\alpha}}}\cdot\frac{1}{i^{\alpha}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the negative logarithm, the self-information of <math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded from below:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{SI}(t_{i},\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})=-\log\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\geq\log(\hskip-8.99994pt\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\hskip-8.99994pt{i^{\alpha}}/{j^{\alpha}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>SI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{SI}(t_{i},\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})=-\log\Pr(t_{i}\mid\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\geq\log(\hskip-8.99994pt\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\hskip-8.99994pt{i^{\alpha}}/{j^{\alpha}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, the RTF-SI satisfies:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{RTF\text{-}SI}(D,t_{i},\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\geq\frac{n_{D}(t_{i})}{\sum_{D^{\prime}\in\mathbb{D}}n_{D^{\prime}}(t_{i})}\cdot\log(\hskip-8.99994pt\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\hskip-8.99994pt{i^{\alpha}}/{j^{\alpha}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>RTF</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>SI</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝔻</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>D</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>min</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><msup><mi>i</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>j</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{RTF\text{-}SI}(D,t_{i},\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}})\geq\frac{n_{D}(t_{i})}{\sum_{D^{\prime}\in\mathbb{D}}n_{D^{\prime}}(t_{i})}\cdot\log(\hskip-8.99994pt\sum_{j=x_{\textup{min}}+1}^{|\mathcal{V}_{\text{target}}|}\hskip-8.99994pt{i^{\alpha}}/{j^{\alpha}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">This theorem allows an adversary to approximate the RTF-SI using its lower bound under a power-law distribution.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
